WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.720
The upcoming Disney+ series The Mandalorian
takes place during an unexplored time period

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.200
in the Star Wars universe.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.700
It's set five years after Return of the Jedi,
and will serve as a bridge between that film

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.020
and The Force Awakens.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:18.040
Since the time gap that separates those two
films is 30 years, there are bound to be plenty

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.620
of revelations mixed into The Mandalorian.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.280
And apparently, fans won't have to wait long
to experience at least one of them: according

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.460
to The New York Times, The Mandalorian's very
first episode contains a major spoiler.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:35.200
The Times didn't reveal what the spoiler is,
but it did say this in a throwaway line tucked

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.040
in a lengthy article about the impending November
12 launch of Disney+:

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:44.219
"The Mandalorian, which contains a dramatic
Star Wars universe spoiler in the first episode

00:00:44.219 --> 00:00:48.629
and will be available the moment Disney Plus
starts, has been as heavily promoted as a

00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:53.829
traditional feature film, with billboards,
30-second television commercials, radio spots

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:55.120
and digital ads."

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:59.700
The show's time frame offers up some tantalizing
possibilities about the bombshell spoiler

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:00.719
that awaits.

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:05.541
By taking place between the fall of the Empire
and the rise of the First Order, The Mandalorian

00:01:05.541 --> 00:01:08.440
is primed to show how the First Order came
to be.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:11.260
As show creator Jon Favreau told Entertainment
Weekly,

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.680
"What could happen in the 30 years between
celebrating the defeat of the Empire and then

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:16.540
the First Order?

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.600
You come in on Episode VII, [the First Order
are] not just starting out.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.480
So somehow, things weren't necessarily managed
as well as they could have been if [the galaxy]

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.280
ended up in hot water again like that."

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:31.660
Contrary to the rumors that swirled when the
series was first announced, according to the

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:35.140
show's creators, The Mandalorian is not about
Boba Fett.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.730
Lead actor Pedro Pascal plays an as-yet unnamed
Mandalorian bounty hunter who operates in

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.640
the seedy outer rim of the galaxy.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:47.220
Carl Weathers portrays Greef Carga, the head
of a bounty hunting guild and an occasional

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:52.760
ally of the Mandalorian, while Giancarlo Esposito
plays a former Imperial Governor named Moff

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:53.260
Gideon.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:59.240
Werner Herzog's character is a crime boss,
Taika Waititi voices droid IG-11, and Gina

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.280
Carano plays ex-Rebel Shock Trooper and current
mercenary Cara Dune.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.420
They, too, will cross paths with the Mandalorian
in their own unique ways.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:12.140
Perhaps the most obvious spoiler is that the
series' crew has been bamboozling us all along,

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:15.760
and the show really is about Boba Fett or
someone related to him.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:22.620
"The gloved, Mandalorian armor gauntlet of
Boba Fett grabs onto the sand outside of the

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.120
Sarlacc pit..."

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:28.080
But it's hard to see the universe-wide implications
of that, despite some fans' desire to see

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:28.580
it.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:35.360
"...and we realize that he survived his fall
during the battle at Jabba's Palace ship."

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.959
Maybe the first episode of The Mandalorian
could offer a spoiler that helps set up The

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.140
Rise of Skywalker.

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:45.940
The series premieres on November 12, and Star
Wars Episode IX opens in theaters December

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:46.440
20.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.000
That gives fans plenty of time to catch The
Mandalorian before watching the film, so if

00:02:51.019 --> 00:02:56.060
the series, say, reveals how Emperor Palpatine
survived the destruction of the second Death

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:00.669
Star, fans would be extremely motivated to
pony up for a full Disney+ subscription to

00:03:00.669 --> 00:03:02.660
watch the show before seeing the movie.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:07.799
Disney has already hinted at seeding its upcoming
MCU offerings on Disney+ with story beats

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.360
that will affect later films.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:14.230
Namely, the streaming series WandaVision is
set to tie into the film Doctor Strange in

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:15.440
the Multiverse of Madness.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.160
Hey, wait a minute…

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:22.500
"If he holds the Reality Gem, that means he
can jump from different realities.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:27.560
This will be our link to the Marvel Universe
from the Star Wars universe!"

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.040
Eh, probably not.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:33.220
The other big possibility is renewed canon
from the old Expanded Universe.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:38.680
Some fans think Mara Jade, Luke Skywalker's
wife in the EU, may be in The Mandalorian,

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.950
and Favreau didn't exactly deny it when asked
about it.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.240
He told EW in September 2019,

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:48.160
"I don't want to talk about anything that
might be fun for people to discover [...] Part

00:03:48.169 --> 00:03:51.879
of what's fun to see if we could merge the
worlds of the original trilogy, the prequels,

00:03:51.879 --> 00:03:57.049
the sequels, The Clone Wars, and what's been
considered canon up to this point and what's

00:03:57.049 --> 00:03:58.500
been considered part of Legends.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.400
I think this show offers an opportunity to
bring in all those elements."

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:06.879
The only way to know for certain what this
big Star Wars spoiler truly is would be to

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.720
tune into the debut episode of The Mandalorian,
hitting Disney+ on November 12.

